  "synonym_discrimination": {
    "words": [
      "type-n",
      "kind-n",
      "sort-n"
    ],
    "note": "All three mean a group of things or people that are alike. **Kind** is the most common in everyday speech: *What kind of food do you like?* **Sort** is a little more informal: *all sorts of things*. **Type** is common in speech too, and it is the usual choice in technical and written English: *What type of battery does it take?*"
  },
